Whilst I accept Sebastian's comments, my problem is slightly different.

I use (in this context) A5 pages with 2 columns and point size 9 on 9.67.
Therefore when I include an image of say 50mm, I can accept a small amount of
whitespace above or below to ensure the baselines of the two columns are
aligned.

I accept that there are wider issues but would like to think that LaTeX3
could address the general principle of providing aligned baselines
(perhaps as on option which can be switched on/off).

Peter


